course: dictionary
lesson: 6146
title: A word with a mill inside
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A miller is a person who works in a mill, grinding grain into flour. Context helps you find this meaning. «Before a loaf of bread reaches you, many people work on it: a farmer grows wheat, a miller grinds flour, a baker bakes.» The farmer grows the wheat and the baker bakes the bread, so the miller must be the one who turns the grain into flour.
explain: Long ago, a miller worked at a windmill or a watermill in the village. The wind or the flowing water turned the mill wheel, and the wheel turned the stones that ground the grain. Many fairy tales have a miller or a miller's daughter in them, such as Rumpelstiltskin.
explain: Miller can also be a family name, like Smith or Baker. The name often came from the job a family's ancestor did. So when you see Miller on a letter or a book cover, it is probably a person's name, not a job.
fact: A miller is a person who owns or works in a mill.
fact: A mill grinds grain into flour.
fact: Windmills are turned by the wind, and watermills are turned by flowing water.
fact: «Meunier, tu dors» is a French song that means «Miller, you are sleeping».
fact: Miller is also a common family name, and it comes from the old job of grinding grain.
exercise: «Before a loaf of bread reaches you, many people work on it: a farmer grows wheat, a miller grinds flour, a baker bakes.» What does a miller do? | Bakes loaves in an oven | *Grinds grain into flour | Grows wheat in a field | Sells bread in a shop
exercise: In the same bread sentence, which person bakes the loaf? | a shopkeeper | *a baker | a farmer | a miller
exercise: A letter is signed «Ella Miller». What is Miller most likely to be here? | a type of bread | a windmill sail | *a family name | a kind of wheat
test: «Meunier, tu dors» is a French song. Which French word means miller? | Tu | *Meunier | Dors | Tu dors
test: In many fairy tales a miller or a miller's daughter appears. Where did a miller usually work? | In a school | On a ship at sea | *At a windmill or watermill in the village | In a castle kitchen
exam: Which word means a person who grinds grain into flour? | Baker | Farmer | *Miller | Driver
